drbd (9.2.19~flant.14-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix permanent quorum loss after a Primary-node reboot. During post-reboot multi-source recovery a peer-state update can ask a node already in L_SYNC_TARGET to re-enter L_WF_BITMAP_T; end_state_change() returns SS_RESYNC_RUNNING and receive_state() treated it as fatal (goto fail -> disconnect), collapsing every replica to Outdated with no UpToDate copy so quorum-minimum-redundancy can never be met (resource stuck forever). receive_state() now postpones the WF_BITMAP re-entry (resync_again++) and keeps the connection, mirroring the receive_bitmap handler. Stock LINBIT path. Companion to flant.12/flant.13. See stress/results/run-14.

 -- Flant <aleksandr.stefurishin@flant.com>  Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0300

drbd (9.2.19~flant.13-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix stuck resync after reboot: the paused source of a multi-source resync is not resumed. When a node becomes UpToDate, __cancel_other_resyncs() cancels the other paused resyncs to L_ESTABLISHED without re-driving them, so a peer that is itself still behind (Outdated/Inconsistent) is left Established with a dirty bitmap and never resyncs. __cancel_other_resyncs() now re-drives such a still-behind peer as SOURCE (resync_again++ + source mask). Companion to the flant.12 oos change. See stress/results/run-13.

 -- Flant <aleksandr.stefurishin@flant.com>  Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:43:00 +0300

drbd (9.2.19~flant.12-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix stuck resync after reboot during bitmap (metadata) exchange: the flant oos==0 guard in resync_again() (6fe5d9dd9) dropped a postponed WF_BITMAP_S/T re-entry needed for data-generation (UUID) reconciliation after a re-handshake, so the sync target waited forever in L_WF_BITMAP_T while the source stayed L_ESTABLISHED. The oos==0 skip now applies only when there is no sync direction (L_ESTABLISHED); a pending WF_BITMAP re-entry proceeds regardless of oos. The corruption guard from 6fe5d9dd9 in drbd_resync_finished() is unchanged.

 -- Flant <aleksandr.stefurishin@flant.com>  Thu, 23 Jul 2026 03:21:00 +0300

drbd (9.2.19~flant.11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix multi-source resync conflict deadlock (cancel-on-pause): when a device resyncs from two peers and drbd_select_sync_target() pauses one to L_PAUSED_SYNC_T, its already-sent resync request never completes (resync-suspended:peer) and blocks the active source's resync of the same block, freezing the resync at done:X% (~5% of replicas after a node reboot). drbd_cancel_paused_resync_requests() drops the paused peer's dangling requests and releases the parked writes.

 -- Flant <aleksandr.stefurishin@flant.com>  Thu, 23 Jul 2026 02:41:00 +0300

drbd (9.2.19~flant.10-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix bitmap leak in drbd_adm_attach() on early attach failure: free device->bitmap on the attach error paths so a replica does not get permanently stuck Diskless with "already has a bitmap, this should not happen" (backport of the fix shape from upstream 9.3.3 commit 8c279459a)

 -- Flant <aleksandr.stefurishin@flant.com>  Thu, 09 Jul 2026 20:42:59 +0300

drbd (9.2.19~flant.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix dagtag-dependent resync stall after Primary reconnect (always send P_DAGTAG; release dagtag waiters on write completion)

 -- Flant <aleksandr.stefurishin@flant.com>  Tue, 23 Jun 2026 22:44:28 +0300

